    "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
    "text": "<p>The Ignite technique may reduce operative time, cost, surgical risks, and morbidity compared to traditional autograft harvesting.<sup>1</sup></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Minimally invasive aspiration and injection</li>\n<li>Ideal for outpatient procedures&nbsp;<br>\n</li>\n<li>No iliac crest harvest complications and cost<br>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The combination of DBM and BMA has over a decade of clinical use. This composite has demonstrated clinical success comparable to open, autologous grafting.<sup>2</sup></p>\n",
    "jcr:lastModified": "Fri Feb 18 2022 20:21:49 GMT+0000",
    "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
    "textIsRich": "true"
  },
